WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.444
Unicode assigns code points to characters.

00:00:02.444 --> 00:00:06.925
UTF-8 is one encoding that turns those code points into bytes.

00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:14.666
The number of characters, code points and bytes can differ; a visible character may also contain multiple code points.

00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:17.110
This matters when storing Indian-language text.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.659
Their code points can require different numbers of UTF-8 bytes.

00:00:21.659 --> 00:00:26.272
For example A uses one byte while the check mark ✓ uses three.

00:00:26.272 --> 00:00:30.885
Size limits should specify whether they count bytes, code points or displayed characters.

00:00:31.885 --> 00:00:35.172
Which converts a Python string to UTF-8 bytes?

00:00:35.172 --> 00:00:38.870
encode creates a byte representation using the selected encoding.
